5. REVIEW C N1 JUDGEMENT
N1 describes a real visual effect: at viewports of 1169 px and above a phone card renders about 576 CSS px
wide against a 520 px source, so the browser upscales roughly 11 percent. It is not a sharpness defect that a
test or a copy change must fix. Spec D-14 states a vitest cannot read pixels, and 520 px is the largest delivered
phone source, so no code change here adds detail. Spec open question 6 and test-strategy section 8.1 record that
Daniel accepts the softness or PR captures again. N1 is a page-check judgement for the PM in task 2.5, or an
owner decision to recapture. No Playwright sharpness test was added.

